That seems significantly less useful than having a term for "noble gases",
especially since nitrogen is actually not as inert as everyone intuitively
thinks--under very high pressure, gas tanks for human breathing need to use
noble gases rather than nitrogen, because under sufficient pressure
diatomic nitrogen begins reacting with our tissues.

